WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:02.824
Mole ran past the rabbit.

2
00:00:02.825 --> 00:00:05.835
The old rabbit fell over.

3
00:00:05.836 --> 00:00:09.008
The other rabbits came out of their holes.

4
00:00:09.009 --> 00:00:11.862
They grumbled at the old rabbit.

5
00:00:11.863 --> 00:00:15.916
"You should have yelled louder!" a gray rabbit said.

6
00:00:15.917 --> 00:00:19.898
"You should have been bold!" said a small one.

7
00:00:19.899 --> 00:00:26.848
"You should have told him the rules," said a rabbit with a red ribbon.

8
00:00:26.849 --> 00:00:29.488
But Mole didn't care.

9
00:00:29.489 --> 00:00:33.332
"What a fine day for running!" said Mole.

10
00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:35.993
Suddenly he stopped.

11
00:00:35.994 --> 00:00:38.668
"What's this?" asked Mole.

12
00:00:38.669 --> 00:00:43.571
He saw something new. A river!

13
00:00:43.572 --> 00:00:45.978
He sat on the riverbank.

14
00:00:45.979 --> 00:00:50.480
"The water is so blue!" said Mole.

15
00:00:50.481 --> 00:00:54.744
"How the waves sparkle!"

16
00:00:54.745 --> 00:00:57.409
Mole looked across the water.

17
00:00:57.410 --> 00:01:00.907
There was a hole in the other riverbank.

18
00:01:00.908 --> 00:01:05.526
"What a cozy place to live!" Mole said.

19
00:01:05.527 --> 00:01:09.028
A small face popped out of the hole.

20
00:01:09.029 --> 00:01:10.916
It was the Water Rat.

21
00:01:10.917 --> 00:01:15.936
"Hello, Mole!" said Water Rat, waving his hand.

22
00:01:15.937 --> 00:01:19.025
"Hello, Rat!" said Mole.

23
00:01:19.026 --> 00:01:22.232
"Would you like to come over?" asked Rat.

24
00:01:22.233 --> 00:01:25.631
"Of course," said Mole happily.

25
00:01:25.632 --> 00:01:29.195
Rat stepped into a little boat by his hole.

26
00:01:29.196 --> 00:01:33.107
He rowed over to Mole.

27
00:01:33.108 --> 00:01:35.519
"Step in!" said Rat.

28
00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:39.617
"This is my first time in a boat!" cried Mole.

29
00:01:39.618 --> 00:01:41.666
Rat was surprised.

30
00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:49.175
"What? Well! Nothing is as great as being in a boat!"

